course: dictionary
lesson: 11556
title: Anaesthesia: medicine that stops pain
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Anaesthesia is a medical word. It means medicine that stops a person feeling pain during an operation. «The surgeon gave Sam anaesthesia before she cut open his arm.» Sam felt no pain, so anaesthesia must be the medicine that stops it.
explain: There are two kinds. General anaesthesia puts a person to sleep, so they feel nothing at all. «Mum had general anaesthesia for her knee operation.» Local anaesthesia only numbs one small part of the body, and the person stays awake.
explain: The word can also mean a loss of feeling in the body. Look at the clues around it. If a hand is numb and cannot feel a pin, that is a loss of feeling. Check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
fact: Anaesthesia is the UK spelling. In US English it is spelled anesthesia.
fact: «Anaesthesia» means medicine that stops a person feeling pain during an operation.
fact: «General anaesthesia» puts a person to sleep, so they feel nothing.
fact: «Local anaesthesia» numbs one part of the body, and the person stays awake.
fact: Anaesthesia can also mean a loss of feeling in the body.
exercise: «The surgeon gave Sam anaesthesia before the operation, so he felt no pain.» What does anaesthesia mean here? | A kind of surgical knife | A loud noise in the operating room | *Medicine that stops a person feeling pain | A hospital bed with wheels
exercise: «The dentist used local anaesthesia, so my mouth went numb but I stayed awake.» Which part of the body was numbed? | The whole body, so I fell asleep | My ears and eyes | *Only one small part | My hair
exercise: «Mum had general anaesthesia for her knee operation.» What does general anaesthesia do? | Makes her knee stronger for ever | Numbs her knee and she stays awake | *Puts her to sleep so she feels nothing | Helps her run faster
test: Which kind of anaesthesia puts a person fully to sleep? | Local | *General | Dental | Mild
test: Dad says, «The anaesthesia has worn off, so my toe can feel again.» What does this tell you? | The anaesthesia was a type of sleeping bag | The anaesthesia made his toe grow longer | *The anaesthesia had removed feeling from his toe for a while | The anaesthesia was a shoe he wore
exam: Which sentence uses anaesthesia correctly to mean medicine that stops pain? | *The nurse gave him anaesthesia so he felt no pain during the operation. | He ate anaesthesia for his lunch. | The anaesthesia was very tall and blue. | The anaesthesia was a red bus that took him home.
